---
import Section from "./Section.astro";
import Footnote from "./Footnote.astro";
---

<Section
  id="different"
  tone="muted"
  eyebrow="The bet"
  title="Where ARK is different."
  lead="Most of what a records system does is settled. These are the three places ARK is built differently, and all three would be hard to reverse later."
>
  <div class="mt-14 space-y-6">
    <article class="reveal rounded-2xl border border-border bg-card p-7 sm:p-10">
      <div class="grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,7fr)_minmax(0,5fr)] lg:gap-14">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">01</p>
          <h3 class="mt-3 text-2xl text-balance">Pricing does not count users.</h3>
          <p class="mt-4 text-muted-foreground">
            This sector runs on volunteers, students, weekend keepers and one person who comes in on
            Tuesdays. Software that prices by user teaches an organization to share a login, and a
            shared login destroys the one thing a record needs: knowing who wrote it.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-4 text-muted-foreground">
            ARK's limits are active animals and storage. There is no seat cap anywhere in the
            product.
          </p>
        </div>

        <aside class="rounded-xl border border-border bg-muted/70 p-6">
          <p class="text-sm font-semibold">For comparison, from their own published pricing</p>
          <dl class="mt-4 space-y-4 text-sm">
            <div>
              <dt class="font-medium">OERCA</dt>
              <dd class="text-muted-foreground">
                Priced per user - publicly quoted at $110 per month for five users, plus a $250
                setup fee.
              </dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt class="font-medium">Tracks</dt>
              <dd class="text-muted-foreground">
                Priced by full-time-equivalent staff.<Footnote id="oerca" />
              </dd>
            </div>
          </dl>
          <p class="mt-5 border-t border-border pt-4 text-sm text-muted-foreground">
            Under ARK, a rescue with forty weekend volunteers pays what a rescue with four pays.
          </p>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="reveal rounded-2xl border border-border bg-card p-7 sm:p-10">
      <div class="grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,7fr)_minmax(0,5fr)] lg:gap-14">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">02</p>
          <h3 class="mt-3 text-2xl text-balance">The phone is the primary surface.</h3>
          <p class="mt-4 text-muted-foreground">
            The incumbents are not standing still here: ZIMS shipped mobile data entry with QR codes
            at the enclosure in May 2026. The difference is which end the system was designed from.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-4 text-muted-foreground">
            ARK was built phone-first and then given a desk view, so nothing on the phone is a
            cut-down version of a screen that lives somewhere else.
          </p>
        </div>

        <figure class="rounded-xl border border-border bg-muted/70 p-6">
          <blockquote>
            <p class="font-display text-lg leading-snug">
              &ldquo;While not all modules are fully supported on mobile&hellip; For the best
              experience, we still recommend using a desktop for more complex tasks.&rdquo;
            </p>
          </blockquote>
          <figcaption class="mt-4 text-sm text-muted-foreground">
            Species360's own documentation, on ZIMS mobile support.<Footnote
              id="species360-mobile"
            />
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="reveal rounded-2xl border border-border bg-card p-7 sm:p-10">
      <div class="grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,7fr)_minmax(0,5fr)] lg:gap-14">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">03</p>
          <h3 class="mt-3 text-2xl text-balance">Import is free, and an admin can run it.</h3>
          <p class="mt-4 text-muted-foreground">
            Most of the cost of changing records systems is the migration nobody has time for, not
            the subscription. Upload a CSV or a spreadsheet, map the columns, see a full preview of
            what would be created, and only then commit.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-4 text-muted-foreground">
            It ships with documented recipes for AnimalCare and ZIMS exports, and it is safe to run
            twice - a row that already exists is skipped and says so, matched on the strongest
            identifier it has.
          </p>
        </div>

        <aside class="rounded-xl border border-border bg-muted/70 p-6">
          <p class="text-sm font-semibold">Where ARK does not replace ZIMS</p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground">
            ZIMS sits on a shared global species database that hundreds of institutions contribute
            to. If participating in that network is why you use it, ARK does not replace it.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground">
            ARK holds the record you keep about the animals in your own care.
          </p>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
</Section>
